Source: socksdirect
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: SocksDirect Maintainers <socksdirect@example.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake (>= 3.16),
               libibverbs-dev,
               libmemcached-dev,
               libnuma-dev,
               python3
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/anthropics/socksdirect

Package: socksdirect
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         libibverbs1,
         socksdirect-monitor (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Fast and compatible user-space sockets — preload library
 SocksDirect is a drop-in BSD socket replacement that bypasses the
 kernel for both intra-host (shared memory) and inter-host (RDMA)
 transports. This package ships libsd.so for use via LD_PRELOAD.

Package: socksdirect-monitor
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         libibverbs1,
         adduser
Description: Fast and compatible user-space sockets — monitor daemon
 The trusted daemon that handles control-plane operations (connection
 establishment, port allocation, fork bookkeeping) for SocksDirect.
 Required by the socksdirect package.

Package: socksdirect-tools
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Fast and compatible user-space sockets — operator tools
 Ships the socksdirect-ctl CLI for inspecting and managing a running
 monitor. Optional.

Package: socksdirect-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         dkms,
         libc6-dev,
         build-essential
Description: Fast and compatible user-space sockets — DKMS kernel module
 Out-of-tree kernel module that exposes /dev/socksdirect for the
 page-remap zero-copy fast path. Without it, libsd falls back to
 memcpy mode for messages >= 16 KiB.
